      <!-- Left: Story + Explanation -->
      <div class="col-md-5">
        <p class="description">03 / Database and data dictionary design</p>

        <h2>Building the Foundation</h2>

        <p>
          The database structure evolved throughout development as the
          website's content and features were refined. Several key decisions
          supported the e-commerce experience.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>Shopping Cart</h3>
          <p>
            Temporary changes to items in the shopping cart are stored in the
            <code>shopping_cart</code> table before the order is confirmed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>Order History</h3>
          <p>
            Orders are divided into <code>order</code> and
            <code>order_detail</code> tables. I joined the
            <code>users</code> table with <code>order</code>, then connected
            it with <code>order_detail</code> to ensure updates could be
            reflected in the Order History page within the Account Center.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>Database Integration</h3>
          <p>
            I also set up routes to fetch data from the database using SQL,
            connecting the backend data with the website interface.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: ER Diagram -->
      <div class="col-md-7">
        <div class="detail-section-image">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="lightbox-trigger"
            data-lightbox-target="er-diagram"
            aria-label="Enlarge Eleganza ER diagram"
          >
            <img
              src="/assets/images/ER_Model.jpg"
              alt="Eleganza database ER diagram"
            />
          </button>

          <p class="description mt-3">
